# SECTION A — TEMPLATE A

## Operational Event System + Project Controls Core

---

## A1. Microservice: Operational Event Ingestion Service (OEIS)

Purpose:
Handle all real-time manual activity inputs across departments.

Responsibilities:

* Validate event payload against Schema Registry
* Persist event in Event Ledger
* Trigger workflow engine
* Trigger agent notifications
* Trigger metric recalculation
* Update Knowledge Graph

---

## A2. Event Ledger (Immutable)

Table: EventLedger

Fields:

* EventID
* Department
* EventType
* LinkedProjectID
* LinkedCustomerID (optional)
* LinkedSupplierID (optional)
* Payload (JSON structured)
* Status (Draft / Submitted / Pending / Approved / Executed / Closed)
* CreatedBy
* Timestamp
* ApprovalStatus
* RiskScore
* VersionHash

All business activity must pass through this table.

---

## A3. Schema Registry (Dynamic Form Engine)

Table: DepartmentSchemas

Hierarchy:
Department
→ EventType
→ Fields
- FieldName
- DataType
- SourceTable (if dropdown)
- Required
- ValidationRules
- ApprovalRequired
- RiskWeight
- WorkflowID

Forms must be generated dynamically from schema.

Cascading dropdown logic required.

Example:
Category → Vaccine → Type → Batch → Quantity

No hardcoded forms.

---

## A4. Workflow Orchestration Engine

State Model:
Draft → Submitted → Pending → Approved → Executed → Closed

Workflow Definition Fields:

* TriggerRoles
* ApprovalRoles
* EscalationTimer
* EscalationRole
* AffectedDepartments
* NotificationPolicy

Must track:

* Who has approved
* Who hasn’t
* Time elapsed
* Bottleneck detection

---

## A5. Role-Based Access Model

Admin Roles:
CEO / CFO / CO

* Full system access
* Override capabilities
* Full AI function access

Department Roles:

* Access limited to department dashboards
* Event logging
* Relevant approvals
* Limited AI tool calls

Staff Dashboard:

* Personal activity feed
* Assigned tasks
* Pending approvals
* KPI contribution
* Achievement/badge system (V1 basic)

RBAC must be enforced server-side.

---

## A6. Reconciliation Engine (Sage Sync)

Bi-weekly import from accounting software.

Process:

1. Import snapshot
2. Normalize financial data
3. Compare against operational records
4. Flag discrepancies
5. Notify Finance
6. Lock reconciliation snapshot
7. Begin new operational cycle

Rule:
Synbot does not overwrite financial core.
It reconciles and reports.

